<title>HONG KONG: K&amp;P Int'l debuts at HK$1.00 per share.</title>
<headline>K&amp;P Int'l debuts at HK$1.00 per share.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of electronics firm K&amp;P International Holdings Ltd made their trading debut on Thursday at HK$1.00 per share, unchanged with their issue price.</p>
<p>K&amp;P offered 55 million new shares at HK$1.00 each in an initial public offering (IPO) with one warrant issued for every five shares. Its IPO was 13.1 times subscribed.</p>
<p>The company makes conductive silicone rubber keypads, electronic calculators, alarm clocks and plastic products.</p>
<p>It said net proceeds would be used to build a new factory in China, acquire additional machinery and support the group's vertical diversification into the production of alarm clock components.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
